{"id":"bastante","lemma":"bastante","pos":"adv","rank":277,"glosses":["quite, rather, pretty, fairly","enough; sufficiently","quite a bit; to a considerable degree"],"ipa":"/basˈtante/","audio":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/43/LL-Q1321_%28spa%29-Marreromarco-bastante.wav","examples":[{"text":"¿Habéis comido bastante?","en":"Have you had enough to eat?","audio":"https://tatoeba.org/en/audio/download/506008","words":[{"g":"to have","l":"haber"},{"g":"having had lunch"},null]},{"text":"Peso bastante más que tú.","en":"I weigh a lot more than you.","audio":"https://tatoeba.org/en/audio/download/451415","words":[{"g":"weight"},null,null,null,{"g":"you"}],"phrases":[[2,4,"apart from"]]},{"text":"Mi trabajo me mantiene bastante ocupado.","en":"My job keeps me pretty busy.","audio":"https://tatoeba.org/en/audio/download/330791","words":[{"g":"my"},{"g":"work, job"},{"g":"me"},{"g":"to keep","l":"mantener"},null,{"g":"occupied"}]},{"text":"Tom me parece bastante normal.","en":"Tom looks pretty normal to me.","audio":"https://tatoeba.org/en/audio/download/801288","words":[null,{"g":"me"},{"g":"to seem, to see fit","l":"parecer"},null,{"g":"normal"}]},{"text":"Nos conocemos bastante bien.","en":"We know each other quite well.","audio":"https://tatoeba.org/en/audio/download/616268","words":[{"g":"us"},{"g":"to know","l":"conocer"},null,{"g":"well"}]}]}